{
  "requirement": "`verify` always captures `Some(criterion.version())`. When `load_evidence` loads\nan older answer with no known version, `Fingerprinted::version()` returns `None`.\n`Record::version` holds the same optional value. In the serialized `revision`\nfield, a concrete string represents `Some(version)` and `\"*\"` represents `None`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.recorded_criterion_version`. I did not read any implementation source.\n\n- **`verify` always captures `Some(criterion.version())`.** `contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` verifies a `Review` and asserts `value.version().unwrap().as_str() == \"v1\"`. After `store_evidence` and `load_evidence`, it asserts `loaded.version() == value.version()`. That shows the captured `Some` version is stored in the `Record` and comes back. The test only uses version \"v1\", but the obligation does not distinguish version values.\n- **`load_evidence` of an older answer with no known version gives `Fingerprinted::version() == None`.** `contracts.rs#fn[wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes]` persists a record, then sets the stored `Record::version` to `None`. It loads with a different revision and asserts `loaded.version() == None`. It also asserts that the requested criterion's version is compatible with the loaded `None` and that `check_inputs` accepts the record.\n- **`Record::version` holds the same optional value.** The stored-record checks above cover this. `storage.rs#fn[record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding]` also deserializes records and asserts `record.version` is `Some(\"review-v1\")` for a concrete string and `None` for `\"*\"`.\n- **Serialized `revision` encoding.** The same storage test round-trips both wire forms and asserts that re-serialization equals the original JSON, so a concrete string stays a string and `None` serializes back to `\"*\"`. It also asserts that `CriterionVersion` itself rejects `\"*\"`, so `\"*\"` cannot be a real version.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation or missing assertion in the subject's text.",
